---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import IconTile from '../../components/IconTile.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../../components/StatusBadge.astro';

// V-477 — trust center landing. Aggregates the customer-trust
// surfaces (security, sub-processors, legal documents, incident
// history) on a single page so customers evaluating the platform
// have one URL to bookmark.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Trust center"
  description="Driftstack trust center: security architecture, sub-processors, legal agreements, incident history, and live platform status. One bookmark for everything compliance-relevant."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <PageHero label="Trust center" title="One bookmark for everything compliance-relevant.">
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-tk-ink-2">
      Security architecture, sub-processor list, legal agreements,
      and incident history — published in one place. Buyer
      evaluations and ongoing GDPR / data-processing-agreement (DPA)
      reviews can start here without
      an email chain.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <StatusBadge />
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <!-- Cards -->
  <section class="relative">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <a href="/security/" class="card group p-6">
          <IconTile class="mb-3">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 2L4 5v6c0 5.5 3.8 10.7 8 11.8 4.2-1.1 8-6.3 8-11.8V5l-8-3z" />
            </svg>
          </IconTile>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tk-accent-text">
            Security
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-tk-ink group-hover:text-tk-accent-text">
            Architecture + posture →
          </h2>
          {/* S26 2026-07-06 (#132) — pillar-count accuracy fix: this
               card said "Five pillars" while /security (the page it
               links to) renders SIX (01 Transport / 02 Egress /
               03 API keys / 04 Webhooks / 05 Team roles / 06
               Live-media handling). The old five-item list also
               counted "EU-resident infrastructure", which is not one
               of the /security pillars — it now rides as its own
               sentence, and the enumeration matches the
               real six. S30 2026-07-07 (founder decision: soften):
               that sentence now says "EU servers" — the six pillars
               run on the EU control plane (true), but blanket
               "EU-resident infrastructure" over-reached since file
               objects live on Cloudflare R2 in the default
               jurisdiction (EU + US replication). */}
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
            Six pillars shipped today: everything between you and us
            travelling encrypted (TLS), profiles able to attach a public
            SOCKS5 exit while profiles without one use managed egress, API keys stored only as
            one-way scrypt hashes (unreadable even to us), webhooks
            cryptographically signed so you can prove each message
            came from us (HMAC), team roles where your whole team can
            look but only admins can change, and live-session media that is
            not retained by default — media is transport-encrypted, and the
            product exposes no administrative staff join path. The API control
            plane and primary database run on EU infrastructure; LiveKit picks
            a media region per session with EU preferred. The live posture
            across each pillar is
            on the security overview (its own card below).
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/trust/sub-processors/" class="card group p-6">
          <IconTile class="mb-3">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2" /><path d="M3 9h18M9 4v16" />
            </svg>
          </IconTile>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tk-accent-text">
            Sub-processors
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-tk-ink group-hover:text-tk-accent-text">
            Live list + regions →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
            Every outside company that handles customer data for us
            (our sub-processors), with where it runs, what it does,
            and the legal basis for any data leaving the EU (the
            transfer mechanism). This list is the official source for
            the 30-day change notices GDPR Article 28(2) requires, and
            it appears verbatim as Annex 3 of our data-processing
            agreement (DPA).
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/trust/incidents/" class="card group p-6">
          <IconTile class="mb-3">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /><path d="M12 7v5l3 2" />
            </svg>
          </IconTile>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tk-accent-text">
            Incident history
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-tk-ink group-hover:text-tk-accent-text">
            Past events + post-mortems →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
            Customer-impacting outages and security incidents, with
            timestamps, customer impact, root cause, and the remediation
            we applied. Live status badge above for current platform
            health.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/legal/dpa/" class="card group p-6">
          <IconTile class="mb-3">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z" /><path d="M14 2v6h6" />
            </svg>
          </IconTile>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tk-accent-text">
            Legal
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-tk-ink group-hover:text-tk-accent-text">
            DPA · Privacy · Terms · AUP →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
            Standard agreements ready to sign on the customer side: Data
            Processing Agreement (GDPR Article 28, including the EU's
            Standard Contractual Clauses — SCCs — for data sent
            abroad), Privacy Policy (the GDPR Article 13–15
            disclosures: what we collect and your rights over it),
            Terms of Service, Acceptable Use
            Policy.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/trust/compliance/" class="card group p-6">
          <IconTile class="mb-3">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M9 11l3 3 8-8" /><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11" />
            </svg>
          </IconTile>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tk-accent-text">
            Compliance
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-tk-ink group-hover:text-tk-accent-text">
            Compliance + disclosure →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
            The attestations available today, how to report a security
            issue privately, our safe-harbour commitment for good-faith
            research, sub-processor change notice, and current log-retention
            periods.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/trust/security-overview/" class="card group p-6">
          <IconTile class="mb-3">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" /><path d="M21 21l-4.35-4.35" />
            </svg>
          </IconTile>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tk-accent-text">
            Security overview
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-tk-ink group-hover:text-tk-accent-text">
            Evaluator's checklist →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
            Every security claim mapped to the code path, test, or
            doc that backs it up. The page your security lead (CISO)
            skims
            before scheduling a vendor review call.
          </p>
        </a>

        <a href="/trust/cumulative-rig/" class="card group p-6">
          <IconTile class="mb-3">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4" /><path d="M7 8h10M7 12h4" />
            </svg>
          </IconTile>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-tk-accent-text">
            Cumulative rig
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold text-tk-ink group-hover:text-tk-accent-text">
            Signal-by-signal methodology →
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
            Every measurable fingerprint signal — the details a
            website can read about a browser — checked one by one
            against a real reference iPhone, shown side by side with
            what a typical disguised-Chromium ("stealth") tool
            returns. The evidence behind our claim that sessions
            can't be told apart from a real iPhone.
          </p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quick-reference strip -->
  <Section
    label="Quick reference"
    title="The questions buyer evaluations always ask."
    class="bg-tk-surface"
  >
    <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-tk-ink">Where is data hosted?</dt>
        {/* S30 2026-07-07 (founder decision: soften) — "EU only" +
            "R2 EU jurisdiction" over-claimed: R2 uses the default
            jurisdiction and replicates EU + US. Compute + database
            are EU-true. */}
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          EU by default. Compute (Hetzner Nuremberg), database (Neon Frankfurt);
          object storage (Cloudflare R2, EU + US replication). Full list at
          <a href="/trust/sub-processors/" class="text-tk-accent-text underline"
            >/trust/sub-processors</a
          >.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-tk-ink">Do you see our destination URLs?</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          Yes, when you send a navigate request or an agent plans one,
          Driftstack's control plane processes the destination URL and
          records the navigation event for your account. The browser's
          destination traffic then leaves through your configured public
          SOCKS5 proxy, or through Driftstack-managed infrastructure when
          the profile has no attached exit.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-tk-ink">Are API keys recoverable by staff?</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          No. Keys are stored only as one-way scrypt hashes — staff,
          and even a database thief, see scrambled values, not keys.
          If a key leaks, rotate it in the dashboard; the old key
          keeps working for 24 hours (the grace window) so nothing
          breaks mid-switch.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-tk-ink">How do we get a DPA on file?</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          The DPA at <a href="/legal/dpa/" class="text-tk-accent-text underline"
            >/legal/dpa</a
          > is already signed by Driftstack — sign your side and it's
          in force. The EU's Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) cover
          any transfer of data outside the EU listed in Annex 3 (the
          vendor list attached to the DPA).
        </dd>
      </div>
      {/* S43 2026-07-07 (founder-approved) — aligned to ToS §9: API
          Scale (self-serve) also carries the contractual SLA, and the
          unverified "self-hosted SKUs carry contractual SLA terms"
          claim is dropped in favour of what the ToS actually grants. */}
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-tk-ink">What's the incident-response SLA?</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          Most plans come without a contractual uptime guarantee
          (an SLA) —
          we publish incidents at
          <a href="/trust/incidents/" class="text-tk-accent-text underline"
            >/trust/incidents</a
          > and the live status above. The API Scale and Enterprise
          tiers carry a contractual SLA (99.9% monthly availability +
          a Severity-1 first-response commitment — see the
          <a href="/docs/sla-policy/" class="text-tk-accent-text underline"
            >SLA policy</a
          >).
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-tk-ink">How do we get a security questionnaire answered?</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-tk-ink-2">
          Email <a href="mailto:support@driftstack.dev" class="text-tk-accent-text underline"
            >support@driftstack.dev</a
          > with the document; we'll fill it line-by-line. Standard
          security-questionnaire formats (CAIQ / VSAQ), custom
          spreadsheets, and vendor portals all welcome.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </Section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <CtaBand
    label="Compliance review"
    title="Bring the questionnaire. We'll fill it."
    lead="Standard security-questionnaire formats (CAIQ, VSAQ) and custom enterprise vendor questionnaires — all welcome. Most answers come from the pages linked above; we answer the remaining items in writing."
    primaryHref="mailto:support@driftstack.dev"
    primaryLabel="Email us"
  />
</BaseLayout>
